# Disable the in-tree KernelSU so Magisk (in the ramdisk) is the only root
# provider. A6rk booted KameOS with CONFIG_KSU=y and the Magisk-patched
# ramdisk, and ended up with NEITHER: `su: inaccessible or not found`,
# /data/adb unreadable, no magisk process. KernelSU needs its own manager app
# to grant anything, and granting requires tapping a UI -- useless for an
# unattended test -- while Magisk's magiskinit did not take over.
# One root provider, and it should be the one already provisioned in /data.
# CONFIG_KSU is not set
